# The govern.json sections whose `rationale` the loader reads, and a rule a
# check refuses under in each (A233, Bundle 21 PR 3).
#
#   path|rule
#
# path  the section, as tools/rationale_sections.py prints it from the
#       loader's parse sites; test_rationale_sections.sh requires the two lists
#       to be the same. In an entry, [] and * stand for the entry the suite
#       writes: custom_rules[] is id r1, governance_plugins[].rules[] id p1,
#       behavioral_sequences.patterns[] pattern p1, contracts.functions.* fn f.
# rule  a rule name the engine enforces under that section -- the name a
#       refusal records and its rationale is looked up by. More rows for one
#       path name the other spellings a check uses below it (aliases,
#       sub-rules), each looked up the same way.
#
# A row means: with `rationale` set at PATH, GovernanceEngine::ruleSectionInfo()
# returns it for RULE (asked through naab-gov context, the read a refusal and
# every report share).
advisory_escalation|advisory_escalation
behavioral_sequences|behavioral_sequences
behavioral_sequences.patterns[]|behavioral_sequences.p1
capabilities.env_vars|capabilities.env_vars
capabilities.filesystem|capabilities.filesystem
capabilities.network|capabilities.network
capabilities.process|capabilities.process
capabilities.shell|capabilities.shell
circuit_breaker|circuit_breaker
